olicyTypes: [\\\"Ingress\\\", \\\"Egress\\\"]\",\"Isolation is defined in NetworkPolicy, Pod Security and service account settings, not in prompt text.\",\"Searched for isolation expressed only in prompts or agent URL/host checks: the model chooses no destination; hosts come from deployment env (deployment.yaml:44-57).\")\nans(\"prescan\",\"H001\",\"--verdict\",\"dismissed\",\"--reason\",\"This is an ERP operation-name allowlist, not a filesystem or network sandbox; the destination is fixed by env. Its over-broad prefixes (invoice., vendor.) let write operations through erp_call, which belongs to B05.\")\nans(\"flag\",\"B08\",\"--evidence\",N+\":75\",\"--note\",\"Egress to 0.0.0.0/0 on 443 and namespace-wide ERP peer\")\nans(\"item\",\"B08\",\"--rating\",\"gap\",\"--confidence\",\"high\",\"--summary\",\"Network policy has default deny but allows all public IPv4 destinations on 443 and the whole ERP gateway namespace.\",\"--next\",\"Remove the 0.0.0.0/0 rule, route egress only through the proxy, and add a podSelector to the ERP gateway rule.\",\"--violates\",\"no path to unapproved production resources, admin systems, host services, or other tenants\",\"--also-affects\",\"B09\")\n# ---- B09\ncheck(\"B09.1\",\"no\",N+\":75\",\"cidr: 0.0.0.0/0\",\"Egress to 0.0.0.0/0 on TCP 443 is allowed, so outbound is not allowlisted at the network layer; the proxy allowlist (lines 109-112) is only used by clients that honor HTTPS_PROXY.\")\ncheck(\"B09.2\",\"no\",D+\":58\",\"- name: HTTPS_PROXY\",\"The proxy is selected by an env var only, and networkpolicy.yaml:73-82 lets pods reach the internet on 443 directly, so the proxy can be bypassed. NO_PROXY is only .svc.cluster.local.\")\ncheck(\"B09.3\",\"unknown\",N+\":80\",\"- 169.254.0.0/16\",\"IPv4 metadata is excepted in the network policy and app clients set follow_redirects=False (payments.py:28, slack.py:35, mcp_client.py:73), but resolved-IP and IPv6 checks would live in the platform egress proxy outside this repo.\")\ncheck(\"