{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDe9NKpzH8Fcwh93WKJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the results in `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validation (`--batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges`) passed. I did not run challenges and did not add any other items. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | `find_valid` (`app/approvals.py:71-92`) matches only tool, target, tenant, status and expiry. It never compares the requesting instance or the args hash. There is no scope column. An approval is never marked used, so it can be replayed for its 60-minute TTL and by parallel calls. `gate.py` does not recheck permissions or resource state when the action runs. B06.5 is `yes`: approval-store errors raise before the tool dispatches. |\n| B07 Hard execution budgets | gap | B07.1 and B07.3 are `yes`. Six finite limits are set in `policy.yaml`. The extractor's child run shares the parent budget and its role cannot spawn further children. B07.2 and B07.4 are `no`: tokens and cost are charged only after the model call returns, and the daily quotas are checked only after spend. The `count_tokens` helper is not metered. `charge_model` can raise before `flush()`, so that call's spend never reaches the quotas. `AsyncAnthropic()` has no explicit timeout, so wall-clock is checked only between turns. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | gap | The network policy has default deny, but `networkpolicy.yaml:75` allows `0.0.0.0/0` on 443. The ERP rule at lines 58-63 allows the whole gateway namespace with no `podSelector`. B08.3 is `yes`: isolation is defined in infrastructure. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | gap | B09.1 and B09.2 are `no`. The proxy is selected only by an env var, and the `0.0.0.0/0` rule lets pods reach the internet directly. B09.3 to B09.5 are `unknown`: resolved-IP and IPv6 checks, tenant or path limits, and block logging and alerts would live in the platform team's proxy. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | needs_evidence | B10.1 to B10.4 are `yes`. The image is pinned by digest, and the Kyverno policy pins the exact keyless issuer and subject. It checks build type, repository, ref, path and builder, and runs in Enforce mode with `failurePolicy: Fail`. B10.5 is `unknown`. CI uses Cosign v2.6.2, which meets the minimum. The verifier that actually runs at admission is Kyverno, and its bundled Cosign version isn't shown in the repo. |\n\n**Prescan hits.**\n- H002 is confirmed under B09.\n- H001 and H005 are dismissed. H001 is only an ERP operation-name allowlist, not a path or network sandbox. Its broad `invoice.` and `vendor.` prefixes let write operations through `erp_call` without approval. That belongs to B05, which is outside this batch.\n- H003, H004, H006 and H007 belong to B11 and R05, which are outside this batch, so I left them unresolved.\n\nI also left scratch files in the workspace: `ledgers/` (the scripts and ledger JSON I used), `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":89477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":620},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bab7479-4984-4603-866c-9a46e3ebe0d2","uuid":"7c18a0aa-ed70-4153-ac7e-b90515444786","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:24:17.328Z","request_id":"req_011CgDe9MzjYSkvAFWKiYL9Z"}
